## Example queries

## Data Management

### QAQC

Site IDs must follow the pattern: exp_id_method_### with 3-digit padding
Coordinates validated to ensure they fall within reasonable marine boundaries
Expedition ID must exist in expeditions.info
Method must be from controlled vocabulary (uvs, sbruv, pbruv, edna, sub, birds, dscm)
Dates must fall within expedition start/end dates
No duplicate site IDs allowed

### Update process

Sites are added as each method data pipeline is completed.
Data is validated against expedition metadata before insertion.
Method-specific details are added to respective method tables.
Updates coordinated through central data management team
